// The receive PATTERN is itself a foreign term, with a hole NESTED under two guest binders:
//
//     for( @lambda:Term`lam f. lam x. ${body}` <- @"results" )
//
// It matches only λ-terms of that SHAPE, and binds `${body}` — a SUB-TERM of the foreign term,
// from under both binders — out into Rholang as an ordinary Rholang name. `${x}` is a typed AST
// hole, matched by structure; nothing is spliced as text.
//
// Three terms rest here. Only the first has the shape. The identity and the application do not
// match and are still on @"results" when the program rests.
//
// EXPECT   @"OUT" = ⟦(1 (1 (1 (1 (1 0)))))⟧ — five applications: the BODY of Church 5

@"results"!(lambda:Term`lam f. lam x. (f, (f, (f, (f, (f, x)))))`) |
@"results"!(lambda:Term`lam x. x`) |
@"results"!(lambda:Term`(lam x. x, lam y. y)`) |

for(@lambda:Term`lam f. lam x. ${body}` <- @"results") {
  @"OUT"!(body)
}
